22: ## Authority and delivery scope
23: 
24: This is the governing API integration policy for the current hard cutover. The
25: owner confirmed that deployed consumers and workers do not require compatibility.
26: The target is native oRPC v2 for first-party commands and queries, exclusively at
27: `/api/v1`, without legacy route aliases, declaration converters or a parallel
28: first-party OpenAPI transport. The URL's `v1` is the product API generation; it
29: does not mean oRPC package v1.
30: 
31: The immediate delivery is the **horizontal foundation**: ownership rules, channel
32: boundaries, architecture enforcement and verification. Feature migrations and
33: unresolved product-policy choices are subsequent work. The owner subsequently authorized a hard reset of the API implementation. The
34: current source is a v1 foundation with two read-only identity procedures, not a
35: feature migration or completed API.
36: Passing its architecture gate does not establish feature or authorization coverage.
37: 
38: The user's ERP + LMS + AI/agentic + social + wellbeing description expresses
39: product breadth. It is not a prescribed domain taxonomy. Preserve the
40: [product covenant](../../../../docs/Core/gurudevi-soul-and-core-covenant.md), the
41: [human-first product map](../../../../docs/architecture/2026-10-23-platform-domain-reality-and-human-first-sanctuary-map.md)
42: and existing institutional rules. A principal acts in an institutional or
43: commercial context, never a personal principal workspace. Personal teacher
44: capacity is a distinct case, not permission to invent personal principal authority.
